Level 7 → Level 8

Concept
This level gives you a big text file (data.txt) and tells you the 
password sits on the line next to a specific word ("millionth"). 
With a file that large, scrolling through manually isn't realistic - 
it's testing whether you know how to search text content directly 
instead of opening the whole file.

 Commands used
pwd
find /home/bandit7 -name data.txt
grep millionth data.txt

Why it works
pwd just confirmed where I was before searching. find /home/bandit7 -name data.txt 
located the exact file by name rather than guessing a path. grep then 
searched inside that file for any line containing the word "millionth" 
and printed just that line - since the password was sitting right next 
to that word on the same line, grep pulled it straight out without 
needing to open or scroll through the rest of the file.
